     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Asha's friend lives with grandparents while another lives with parents only.\n\"Families come in many types,\" said her teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "nuclear family",
     "joint family",
     "interdependence"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "A nuclear family has parents and children. A joint family also has grandparents, uncles, aunts and cousins. Some families have a single parent.\nFamily members share duties and care for one another. Communities such as neighbours, schools and villages depend on each other: farmers grow food, teachers teach, doctors heal.\nModern communities include apartments and online groups."
    }
